From d26544689bfbbb81b0c2873f98e592920dcc91ec Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Shashank Jarmale <shashank.jarmale@sentry.io>
Date: Thu, 12 Feb 2026 13:39:40 -0800
Subject: [PATCH] feat(ci): Migrate `black`, `isort`, `pyupgrade`, and most of
 `flake8` to `ruff` (#108010)

Follow-up to https://github.com/getsentry/getsentry/pull/19255/.

Migrating `black`, `isort`, `pyupgrade`, and most of `flake8` to `ruff`.
`ruff` is significantly faster, it's a single unified tool, it's already
an industry standard, and we can count on it improving/evolving at a
much faster rate than these other tools.

View [this
commit](https://github.com/getsentry/sentry/pull/108010/changes/96cea08f1f7cf3c221a475ce1efe5be3c04247fe)
and [this
commit](https://github.com/getsentry/sentry/pull/108010/changes/1503b17ad32bcc5eeb1c838396e8f4c814ed6c65)
for the actual updates. There are also some rule violations manually
fixed in [this
commit](https://github.com/getsentry/sentry/pull/108010/changes/f0c1f0aebccf7c13f984e4b2f7d235b4dd6c37b3).
The other changes are just the results of applying `ruff` linting &
formatting to the codebase. Relevant files:
- `pyproject.toml`
([diff](https://github.com/getsentry/sentry/pull/108010/changes#diff-50c86b7ed8ac2cf95bd48334961bf0530cdc77b5a56f852c5c61b89d735fd711))
- `uv.lock`
([diff](https://github.com/getsentry/sentry/pull/108010/changes#diff-84321598744d84dbee2318e634c74c9aae39a1c253f1c4bd17ebf9ef2f807b11))
- `setup.cfg`
([diff](https://github.com/getsentry/sentry/pull/108010/changes#diff-fa602a8a75dc9dcc92261bac5f533c2a85e34fcceaff63b3a3a81d9acde2fc52))
- `.pre-commit-config.yaml`
([diff](https://github.com/getsentry/sentry/pull/108010/changes#diff-63a9c44a44acf85fea213a857769990937107cf072831e1a26808cfde9d096b9))
- `.vscode/extensions.json`
([diff](https://github.com/getsentry/sentry/pull/108010/changes#diff-c16655a98a3ee89a7636a59c59a72b0e93649e3a1e947327cfc43a1336b4e912))
- `.vscode/settings.json`
([diff](https://github.com/getsentry/sentry/pull/108010/changes#diff-a5de3e5871ffcc383a2294845bd3df25d3eeff6c29ad46e3a396577c413bf357))

Follow-up items:

- [ ] Once this PR is merged, update `.git-blame-ignore-revs` so that
`git blame` will skip over the formatting changes when determining the
original author of code
- [ ] Communicate in #team-engineering that we can use `ruff format` /
`ruff check` instead of `black`/`isort` (and IDE configs/formatters can
be updated)
- [ ] Improve the `ruff` coverage we have in `getsentry`
- [ ] Remove the `exclude = ["bin/"]` from `pyproject.toml` and fix all
the `ruff` errors in `bin/`
- [ ] Add enforcement for "PT" rules with `ruff` in `pyproject.toml` -->
may have to make some fixes to allow this
- [ ] Gradually remove the ignored `ruff` rules in `pyproject.toml` -->
likely will want to fix and remove them one-by-one
- [ ] If possible, remove the `tool.ruff.lint.per-file-ignores` in
`pyproject.toml`
    - [ ] Add enforcement for more `ruff` rules, if desired
- [ ] Improve the `ruff` coverage we have in `sentry`
- [ ] Gradually remove the ignored `ruff` rules in `pyproject.toml` -->
likely will want to fix and remove them one-by-one
    - [ ] Add enforcement for more `ruff` rules, if desired
- [ ] Look into whether we can use `ruff` for custom AST-based linting
in order to replace the `flake8` custom Sentry S* rules (and then
`flake8` can be fully removed as a dependency) --> this may just not yet
be supported by `ruff`
